  "query_preview": "..\nWhile a generally dry period remains through the weekend,\nprecipitable water remains between 1.75\" and 2.25\" across all\nislands. This moisture is expected to remain along with light and\nvariable winds, so island effect showers and isolated thunderstorms \nwill be possible Sunday and Monday. For Sunday, Guam will have the\nhighest chance for significant rainfall. Rota may see some lighter\nshowers. Island-effect showers over Tinian and Saipan will likely \nremain mostly offshore to the west. Weak upper-level support and \nslightly increased shear should allow for some island-effect showers\nto produce lightning and last longer than today. By Monday, all \nislands will likely see afernoon showers and isolated thunderstorms. \nFor Saipan, these showers will likely build over the southwest \nportion of the island due to a weak northeast wind. By Tuesday, \nwesterlies winds ahead of a slowly developing trough may prevent \nfurther island effect showers, but then bring additional monsoon \nmoisture into the region sometime Wednesday. This will bring shower \ncoverage back to scattered with isolated thunderstorms possible. This\ntrough will be closely monitored for any potential impacts to the \nMarianas late next week. Models currently indicate it drifting north \nof the Marianas with a monsoon tail bringing precipitation and breezy\nconditions to the Marianas.",
